<title>SOUTH KOREA: Daesung starts producing gas in U.S..</title>
<headline>Daesung starts producing gas in U.S..</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daesung Industrial Co Ltd said on Tuesday it had jointly begun commercial production of natural gas in southeast Oklahoma, the United States.</p>
<p>A Daesung statement said it had recently discovered commercially-viable deposits in seven test holes at the Maddox field in the Arkoma Basin area. A feasibility study in the field showed recoverable reserves of about four million tonnes of natural gas.</p>
<p>It said Daesung and two U.S. firms, including Texaco Inc, would invest a total of $50 million in the project. Daesung has a 35 percent stake, Texaco 54 percent and another unidentified U.S. firm 11 percent.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
